IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s72-period-of-allowance`
IMPORT `nii-s335-branches`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-part-d`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Independent tests for row IL-08, National Insurance half: s 72, s 335, Schedule A1 Part D.
-- Author: fid-il-08b, 2026-10-07. A first session wrote DECIDED-ANSWERS.md from the Hebrew source,
-- before any module of this encoding was opened, and drafted this file; it was cut off by a usage
-- limit. A second session verified the draft against DECIDED-ANSWERS.md line by line, gave every
-- assertion its scenario id, and replaced partial per-branch checks (335-10, -16 to -20) with the
-- full branch lists decided. No expected value was changed to match the encoding.
-- A failing or refused assertion is a finding (INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md). Scenarios the interface
-- cannot express carry a comment marked NOT EXPRESSIBLE, and are listed there too.
-- Rules used that carry no @export (the first and last month of s 72, the day under Part D) are
-- named in the comment of the assertion that uses them.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Independent tests for row IL-08`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `arose`  IS A DATE
      `ended`  IS A `How the entitlement for the child ended`
      `lived`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
`fid entitlement` `arose` `ended` `lived` `paid` MEANS
    `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72` WITH
        `the day the entitlement arose`                            IS `arose`
        `how it ended`                                             IS `ended`
        `the child lived at least seven days or left the hospital` IS `lived`
        `a child allowance was paid for the child`                 IS `paid`

-- An entitlement that has not ended, for a child who lived seven days.
GIVEN `arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
`fid open from` `arose` MEANS `fid entitlement` `arose` `it has not ended` TRUE TRUE

-- An entitlement that arose long ago and ceased, other than by death, on the given day.
GIVEN `ceased` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
`fid ceased on` `ceased` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2020 1 1) (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` `ceased`) TRUE TRUE

-- An entitlement that arose long ago, for which an allowance was paid, ended by the child's death.
GIVEN `died` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
`fid died on` `died` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2020 1 1) (`the child died on` `died`) TRUE TRUE

-- The exported s 72 rule.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
      e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fid paid` m y e MEANS `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` m `of` y `, for` e

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fid mc` m y MEANS `s 72 — the month count of` m `of` y

-- The first month paid, from the (unexported) s 72(a) rule, which takes no period guard.
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fid first month` e MEANS `s 72(a) — the first month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e

-- The number of months paid, from the encoding's own (unexported) first and last month.
GIVEN e IS AN `An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`fid months paid` e MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 72(a), (c) — the last month for which the allowance is paid, as a month count, for` e
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST l  THEN JUST (l MINUS `fid first month` e PLUS 1)

GIVEN p IS A `A person in a contribution period, for section 335`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
`fid branches` p MEANS `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` p

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fid part D age` d MEANS `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born on` d

-- Unexported: the day she reaches the Part D age.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`fid part D day` d MEANS `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` d

§§ `Section 72(a), first and second limbs: when payment starts`

-- Each: paid for the month expected, and not for the month before.
-- 72-01
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 1))   AND NOT `fid paid` 2 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- 72-02
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 14))  AND NOT `fid paid` 2 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 14))
-- 72-03 (RD-1: the 15th is in the first limb)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 15))  AND NOT `fid paid` 2 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 15))
-- 72-04
#ASSERT `fid paid` 4 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 16))  AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 16))
-- 72-05
#ASSERT `fid paid` 4 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 31))  AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 31))
-- 72-06
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 2 15))  AND NOT `fid paid` 1 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 2 15))
-- 72-07 (last day of February, common year)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 2 28))  AND NOT `fid paid` 2 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 2 28))
-- 72-08 (leap day)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2024 (`fid open from` (YMD 2024 2 29))  AND NOT `fid paid` 2 2024 (`fid open from` (YMD 2024 2 29))
-- 72-09 (leap year, not the last day)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2024 (`fid open from` (YMD 2024 2 28))  AND NOT `fid paid` 2 2024 (`fid open from` (YMD 2024 2 28))
-- 72-10 (across the year)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 1 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2025 12 16)) AND NOT `fid paid` 12 2025 (`fid open from` (YMD 2025 12 16))
-- 72-11 (across the year)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 1 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2025 12 31)) AND NOT `fid paid` 12 2025 (`fid open from` (YMD 2025 12 31))
-- 72-12
#ASSERT `fid paid` 12 2025 (`fid open from` (YMD 2025 12 15)) AND NOT `fid paid` 11 2025 (`fid open from` (YMD 2025 12 15))
-- 72-13 (last day of a 30-day month)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 4 30))  AND NOT `fid paid` 4 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 4 30))
-- 72-14: commencement day of the consolidation (s 402), 1 October 1995: paid from October 1995.
#ASSERT `fid paid` 10 1995 (`fid open from` (YMD 1995 10 1))
-- 72-14, through the unexported s 72(a) first-month rule.
#ASSERT `fid first month` (`fid open from` (YMD 1995 10 1)) EQUALS `fid mc` 10 1995

§§ `Section 72(a), third limb: when payment ends`

-- Each: paid for the month entitlement ceased, and not for the month after. The encoding answers by
-- month, so "last day paid" is asserted as "that month paid, the next not".
-- 72-20
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 1))   AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 1))
-- 72-21
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 15))  AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 15))
-- 72-22 (no 15th-day split on cessation)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 16))  AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 16))
-- 72-23
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 31))  AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 5 31))
-- 72-24 (common-year February)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 2 10))  AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 2 10))
-- 72-25 (leap-year February)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2028 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2028 2 10))  AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2028 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2028 2 10))
-- 72-26 (leap day)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2028 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2028 2 29))  AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2028 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2028 2 29))
-- 72-27
#ASSERT `fid paid` 12 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 12 1)) AND NOT `fid paid` 1 2027 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 12 1))
-- 72-28 (30-day month)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 4 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 4 10))  AND NOT `fid paid` 5 2026 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2026 4 10))
-- 72-29: a 17-year-old marries on 10 June 2025 (s 1 "ילד" excludes a married minor; the caller
-- supplies the day entitlement ceased): June paid, July not.
#ASSERT `fid paid` 6 2025 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2025 6 10))  AND NOT `fid paid` 7 2025 (`fid ceased on` (YMD 2025 6 10))

§§ `Section 72(a) with s 65(a): a child born, and turning 18`

-- The encoding takes the day entitlement ceased as an input; the 18th anniversary (RD-3) is supplied
-- here, so the "turns 18 on" column is not tested. The first month is in 2008, before the export's
-- May 2015 guard, so it is asserted through the unexported s 72(a) rule, and the export is probed
-- once (72-30).
`fid born 2008-05-01` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 5 1)   (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 5 1))   TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2008-05-15` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 5 15)  (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 5 15))  TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2008-05-16` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 5 16)  (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 5 16))  TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2008-05-31` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 5 31)  (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 5 31))  TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2007-12-31` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2007 12 31) (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2025 12 31)) TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2008-01-01` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 1 1)   (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 1 1))   TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2010-02-15` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2010 2 15)  (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2028 2 15))  TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2008-02-28` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 2 28)  (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 2 28))  TRUE TRUE
`fid born 2008-03-01` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 3 1)   (`it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` (YMD 2026 3 1))   TRUE TRUE

-- 72-30: starts May 2008; last May 2026; 217 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2008-05-01` EQUALS `fid mc` 5 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 `fid born 2008-05-01` AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 `fid born 2008-05-01`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2008-05-01` EQUALS JUST 217
-- 72-30, through the exported rule for the first month itself (May 2008).
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2008 `fid born 2008-05-01`
-- 72-31: starts May 2008; last May 2026; 217 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2008-05-15` EQUALS `fid mc` 5 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 `fid born 2008-05-15` AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 `fid born 2008-05-15`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2008-05-15` EQUALS JUST 217
-- 72-32: starts June 2008; last May 2026; 216 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2008-05-16` EQUALS `fid mc` 6 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 `fid born 2008-05-16` AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 `fid born 2008-05-16`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2008-05-16` EQUALS JUST 216
-- 72-33: starts June 2008; last May 2026; 216 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2008-05-31` EQUALS `fid mc` 6 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 5 2026 `fid born 2008-05-31` AND NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 `fid born 2008-05-31`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2008-05-31` EQUALS JUST 216
-- 72-34: starts January 2008; last December 2025; 216 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2007-12-31` EQUALS `fid mc` 1 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 12 2025 `fid born 2007-12-31` AND NOT `fid paid` 1 2026 `fid born 2007-12-31`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2007-12-31` EQUALS JUST 216
-- 72-35: starts January 2008; last January 2026; 217 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2008-01-01` EQUALS `fid mc` 1 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 1 2026 `fid born 2008-01-01` AND NOT `fid paid` 2 2026 `fid born 2008-01-01`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2008-01-01` EQUALS JUST 217
-- 72-36: starts February 2010; last February 2028; 217 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2010-02-15` EQUALS `fid mc` 2 2010
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2028 `fid born 2010-02-15` AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2028 `fid born 2010-02-15`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2010-02-15` EQUALS JUST 217
-- 72-37: starts March 2008; last February 2026; 216 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2008-02-28` EQUALS `fid mc` 3 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2026 `fid born 2008-02-28` AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2026 `fid born 2008-02-28`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2008-02-28` EQUALS JUST 216
-- 72-38: starts March 2008; last March 2026; 217 months.
#ASSERT `fid first month` `fid born 2008-03-01` EQUALS `fid mc` 3 2008
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 `fid born 2008-03-01` AND NOT `fid paid` 4 2026 `fid born 2008-03-01`
#ASSERT `fid months paid` `fid born 2008-03-01` EQUALS JUST 217
-- 72-39, start: born 29 February 2008, paid from March 2008.
#ASSERT `fid first month` (`fid open from` (YMD 2008 2 29)) EQUALS `fid mc` 3 2008
-- 72-39, end: NOT EXPRESSIBLE. Expected REFUSE (RD-4: 28 February or 1 March 2026); the encoding
-- takes the day entitlement ceased as an input, so the caller must choose one and the encoding answers.

§§ `Section 72(b): seven days, or left the hospital`

-- (b) is one boolean input; the caller answers it, the encoding does not count days.
-- 72-40: lived seven days on either count; the caller supplies TRUE.
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 3 8)) TRUE TRUE)
-- 72-41: lived five days, never left hospital: no allowance at all.
#ASSERT NOT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 3 6)) FALSE FALSE)
-- 72-42: NOT EXPRESSIBLE. Expected REFUSE (six days elapsed or seven inclusive); the condition is a
-- boolean input, so the caller must choose and the encoding answers.
-- 72-43: left hospital on day 2, died on day 3: allowance payable for March.
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 3 4)) TRUE TRUE)
-- 72-44: NOT EXPRESSIBLE. Expected "no" on the literal words for a home birth; whether a child never
-- in hospital satisfies (b) is exactly the boolean the caller supplies.
-- 72-45: alive and at home a month later: March and April paid.
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 1)) AND `fid paid` 4 2026 (`fid open from` (YMD 2026 3 1))

§§ `Section 72(c): three months after the month of death`

-- Each: paid to the last month expected, and not after.
-- 72-50
#ASSERT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 3 10))  AND NOT `fid paid` 7 2026 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 3 10))
-- 72-51
#ASSERT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 3 31))  AND NOT `fid paid` 7 2026 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 3 31))
-- 72-52
#ASSERT `fid paid` 7 2026 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 4 1))   AND NOT `fid paid` 8 2026 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 4 1))
-- 72-53 (into a leap February)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2028 (`fid died on` (YMD 2027 11 15)) AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2028 (`fid died on` (YMD 2027 11 15))
-- 72-54
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2027 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 11 15)) AND NOT `fid paid` 3 2027 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 11 15))
-- 72-55 (across the year)
#ASSERT `fid paid` 3 2027 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 12 10)) AND NOT `fid paid` 4 2027 (`fid died on` (YMD 2026 12 10))
-- 72-56: born 10 February 2026, left hospital, died 20 February: February to May paid; not January, not June.
`fid 72-56` MEANS `fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 2 10) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 20)) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `fid paid` 2 2026 `fid 72-56` AND `fid paid` 5 2026 `fid 72-56`
#ASSERT (NOT `fid paid` 1 2026 `fid 72-56`) AND (NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 `fid 72-56`)
-- 72-57: born 20 February 2026 (after the 15th: (a) starts payment in March), left hospital, died
-- 25 February (so (a) ends payment with February). Expected REFUSE for March 2026, whichever way the
-- caller answers "a child allowance was paid for the child".
#ASSERT REFUSED `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 2 20) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 25)) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 2 20) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 2 25)) TRUE TRUE)
-- 72-58: born 20 May 2008, died 10 March 2026, two months before 18: June 2026 paid on the literal words.
#ASSERT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 5 20) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) TRUE TRUE) AND NOT `fid paid` 7 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2008 5 20) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) TRUE TRUE)
-- 72-59: lived three days in hospital: nothing paid, in March or after.
#ASSERT NOT `fid paid` 3 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 3 4)) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `fid paid` 6 2026 (`fid entitlement` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`the child died on` (YMD 2026 3 4)) FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Section 72: before the consolidation commenced`

-- 72-60: entitlement arose 10 January 1995, before s 402's 1 October 1995: REFUSE.
#ASSERT REFUSED `fid paid` 1 1995 (`fid open from` (YMD 1995 1 10))

§§ `Section 335: the branches`

-- Every person below is in a 2026 contribution period. The s 238 statuses (housewife, widow
-- pensioner) and the Chapter statuses are inputs: the caller answers them, the encoding does not.

-- 335-01: resident employee, 30, insured in every Chapter s 335 reads: all nine.
`fid 335-01` MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` WITH
    `the calendar year of the period`                                          IS 2026
    `an employee or a self-employed person`                                    IS TRUE
    `an Israeli resident`                                                      IS TRUE
    `insured under Chapter 11`                                                 IS TRUE
    `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                    IS FALSE
    `a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`                              IS FALSE
    `insured under Chapter 5`                                                  IS TRUE
    `insured under Chapter 6`                                                  IS TRUE
    `insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured in section 158`  IS TRUE
    `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`                      IS FALSE
    `an employee insured under Chapter 8`                                      IS TRUE
    `insured under Chapter 9`                                                  IS TRUE
    `insured for long-term care`                                               IS TRUE
#ASSERT `fid branches` `fid 335-01` EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`

-- 335-02: non-resident employee, insured under Chapters 5 and 8 only: maternity, work injury, insolvency.
`fid 335-02` MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` WITH
    `the calendar year of the period`                                          IS 2026
    `an employee or a self-employed person`                                    IS TRUE
    `an Israeli resident`                                                      IS FALSE
    `insured under Chapter 11`                                                 IS FALSE
    `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                    IS FALSE
    `a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`                              IS FALSE
    `insured under Chapter 5`                                                  IS TRUE
    `insured under Chapter 6`                                                  IS FALSE
    `insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured in section 158`  IS FALSE
    `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`                      IS FALSE
    `an employee insured under Chapter 8`                                      IS TRUE
    `insured under Chapter 9`                                                  IS FALSE
    `insured for long-term care`                                               IS FALSE
#ASSERT `fid branches` `fid 335-02` EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `work injury`, `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`

-- 335-03: non-resident self-employed, insured under Chapter 5 only: maternity, work injury.
`fid 335-03` MEANS `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` WITH
    `the calendar year of the period`                                          IS 2026
    `an employee or a self-employed person`                                    IS TRUE
    `an Israeli resident`                                                      IS FALSE
    `insured under Chapter 11`                                                 IS FALSE
    `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                    IS FALSE
    `a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`                              IS FALSE
    `insured under Chapter 5`                                                  IS TRUE
    `insured under Chapter 6`                                                  IS FALSE
    `insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured in section 158`  IS FALSE
    `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`                      IS FALSE
    `an employee insured under Chapter 8`                                      IS FALSE
    `insured under Chapter 9`                                                  IS FALSE
    `insured for long-term care`                                               IS FALSE
#ASSERT `fid branches` `fid 335-03` EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `work injury`

